    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心發現 toctou 競態條件漏洞，授權攻擊者可進行本地權限提升",
    summary: "本漏洞為 Linux 核心中的 Time-of-check time-of-use (toctou) 競態條件，允許已取得授權的攻擊者在本地環境執行權限提升攻擊。這類競態條件漏洞通常發生在系統檢查某個資源（Time-of-check）與實際使用該資源（Time-of-use）之間存在時間間隙，攻擊者可以在此間隙利用來改變資源的狀態或屬性，從而達到越權或提升權限的目的。由於這是核心層面的漏洞，其影響範圍廣泛，可能導致系統的機密性、完整性與可用性受到嚴重威脅。修補建議是系統維護者應立即更新至修補了此類 toctou 競態條件的 Linux 核心版本，以消除攻擊窗口。由於原文未提供具體 CVE 編號或 CVSS 分數，建議用戶應關注 Linux 發行版（如 Ubuntu, RHEL 等）的官方安全公告，並及時進行核心升級。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "toctou", "競態條件", "權限提升", "CVE-2026-62840"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Discovers toctou Race Condition Vulnerability, Allowing Authorized Attackers Local Privilege Escalation",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability is a Time-of-check time-of-use (toctou) race condition in the Linux kernel, which allows an authorized attacker to perform a local privilege escalation attack within the local environment. Such race condition vulnerabilities typically occur when there is a time gap between the system checking a resource (Time-of-check) and actually using that resource (Time-of-use). An attacker can exploit this gap to change the resource's state or attributes, thereby achieving unauthorized access or privilege elevation. Because this is a kernel-level vulnerability, its impact is widespread, potentially severely threatening the system's confidentiality, integrity, and availability. The recommended fix is for system maintainers to immediately update to a Linux kernel version that has patched this type of toctou race condition to eliminate the attack window. Since the original text did not provide a specific CVE ID or CVSS score, users are advised to monitor official security announcements from Linux distributions (such as Ubuntu, RHEL, etc.) and perform kernel upgrades promptly.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "toctou", "race condition", "privilege escalation", "CVE-2026-62840"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-62840", lang: "EN" }
    ]
