    summary_en: "Apple has released the HomeView smart home display, a 7-inch product priced at $299. It is designed to allow users to control smart accessories, make FaceTime calls, and enjoy video and music content through a single interface. Regarding third-party application support, Apple stated that besides built-in Apple applications (such as Music, Podcasts, and Safari), HomeView will also support 'third-party audio and video applications compatible with iPhone,' providing a familiar cross-device experience. However, detailed information suggests that this functionality appears to primarily rely on the existing CarPlay framework, rather than requiring developers to build dedicated applications for HomeView. Materials from the product launch indicated that some applications may require subscriptions for content access, and some applications require proximity to a paired and compatible iPhone for use. It is currently unclear how the iPhone proximity requirement will function, or whether developers will need to take additional steps to support HomeView, particularly whether the support is limited to media-type applications.",
