    summary_en: "With the release of Gemini 4 Argon, Google has significantly updated the macOS version of the Gemini application by integrating Google's agent-first development platform, Antigravity. Previously a standalone application, Antigravity's functionality is now directly embedded within the Gemini application, aiming to allow users to write applications, web experiences, and more from a single interface. This integration is driven by the enhanced coding capabilities of Gemini 4 Argon. Currently, access to this feature requires the AI Ultra tier within the Gemini application. Additionally, the macOS Gemini application has updated the 'Chat' and 'Tasks' switcher ('Tasks' is the new name for Gemini Spark) and introduced a 'Schedule' view to display Spark tasks and scheduled actions. Furthermore, accessing Skills has transitioned from a slash (/) command to using the @ mention, and the sidebar's 'Custom' feature has replaced Connected Apps, serving as the entry point for Skills and Connectors. Users should ensure they are running the latest version of the Gemini application to access all new features.",
