    title_en: "Samsung's First Android XR Glasses Specs Leak: Featuring Snapdragon AR1 Gen 1 Chip",
    summary_en: "According to leaked information, Samsung's first Android XR glasses will feature the Snapdragon AR1 Gen 1 chip, equipped with 2GB RAM and 64GB storage. The device will also include a 12MP camera (supporting 3K video at 30fps), dual speakers, and a quad-microphone array. The battery life is reported to be 9 hours (up to 72 hours with a charging case), matching the specifications of the latest generation Ray-Ban Meta glasses. In terms of compatibility, the device will support basic functions for Android phones and iPhones, though some Galaxy-exclusive features require the phone to run One UI 9 (Android 17) and the Galaxy Watch to run Wear OS 7. Samsung plans to collaborate with brands such as Gentle Monster and Warby Parker, offering diverse frame styles and color options. While the specific price and release date are unconfirmed, reports suggest a potential launch in November 2026, with rumors even suggesting that the color display version might be delayed until late 2027. The device is expected to reshape the market landscape for wearable computing.",
    tags_en: ["Samsung", "Android XR", "Snapdragon AR1 Gen 1", "XR Glasses", "Wearable Computing", "One UI 9"],
