    summary_en: "Using the Paris Motor Show as a starting point, this article observes trends among European automotive manufacturers. It points out that while the traditional large-scale auto show model is changing, this exhibition demonstrates a renewed trend of manufacturers actively showcasing new vehicles. Stellantis brands, such as Citroen, Peugeot, and Fiat, are the focus. The concept cars displayed, such as the Citroen 2 CV Concept, emphasize 'affordability, lightness, practicality, and versatility,' aiming to provide a more lifestyle-oriented and economical mobility solution. The author also notes that while European design styles carry a retro aesthetic, they question their applicability to the US market, pointing out that some brands still tend toward certain established design trends.",
