    title: "卡斯柏奇在印尼舉辦 SAS 2026：聚焦高階攻擊趨勢與跨域協作",
    summary: "卡斯柏奇（Kaspersky）於印尼巴厘島洲際酒店舉辦「第18屆年度安全分析師峰會」（SAS 2026）。本次峰會以「打破既有框架的網路安全」為主題，預計吸引全球約 200 名參與者。本次活動旨在應對日益複雜的網路威脅環境，強調跨社群合作的重要性。主要議程涵蓋了主要漏洞揭露、多個領域的高階攻擊趨勢分析，以及深入的事件調查結果。特別關注了能規避傳統安全工具的攻擊，並將公開網路情報威脅的研究成果。具體內容包括針對外交機構的 UEFI 啟動區（bootkit）攻擊活動介紹，以及關於 Lazarus APT 組織下一代攻擊戰術的最新研究。此外，峰會還將探討針對消費系統、車載控制系統和公共媒體設備的惡意程式與攻擊案例，以及機器學習與網路安全結合帶來的全新威脅。活動期間，還將舉行 SAS CTF 2026 決賽，共 13 支隊伍參與，爭奪總額 18,000 美元的獎金。",
    tags: ["Kaspersky", "SAS 2026", "網路安全", "UEFI bootkit", "APT", "CTF"],
    title_en: "Kaspersky Hosts SAS 2026 in Indonesia: Focusing on Advanced Attack Trends and Cross-Domain Collaboration",
    summary_en: "Kaspersky is hosting the 18th Annual Security Analyst Summit (SAS 2026) at the InterContinental Bali Bali. This year's summit, themed 'Cybersecurity Beyond Existing Frameworks,' is expected to attract approximately 200 global participants. The event aims to address the increasingly complex cyber threat landscape, emphasizing the importance of cross-community collaboration. Key agenda items include major vulnerability disclosures, advanced attack trend analyses across multiple domains, and in-depth incident investigation findings. Special focus will be placed on attacks capable of bypassing traditional security tools, and research findings on public network intelligence threats will be presented. Specific content includes presentations on UEFI bootkit attacks targeting diplomatic institutions, and the latest research on the next-generation attack tactics of the Lazarus APT group. Furthermore, the summit will explore malware and attack case studies targeting consumer systems, automotive control systems, and public media devices, as well as new threats arising from the integration of machine learning and cybersecurity. During the event, the SAS CTF 2026 finals will also be held, with 13 teams competing for a total prize pool of $18,000.",
